<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of preliminary</p>
<p>round, second leg matches in African club soccer competitions on</p>
<p>Sunday:</p>
<p>Champions' Cup</p>
<p>In Antananarivo: BFV FC (Madagascar) 3 Saint-Michel United</p>
<p>(Seychelles) 0 (halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Taly 2, Nene 14, Piry 84</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000.</p>
<p>BFV win 5-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>African Football Conferation (CAF) Cup</p>
<p>In Addis Ababa: Dire Dawa Locomotive FC (Ethiopia) 0 Simba</p>
<p>FC (Tanzania) 1 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorer: Faw Puller 22</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000.</p>
<p>Simba win 5-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>Cup Winners' Cup</p>
<p>In Harare: Dynamos FC (Zimbabwe) 3 Sigara SC (Tanzania) 0</p>
<p>(2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Ian Gorowa 6, Memory Mucherahowa 32, Llyod Mutasa</p>
<p>58</p>
<p>Attendance: 35,000.</p>
<p>Dynamos win 3-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>CAF Cup</p>
<p>In Kigali: Kiovu (Rwanda) 2 Bata Bullets (Malawi) 1 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Kiovu - Hugo Mukengere 17, Maseraka Beton 82</p>
<p>Bata - Banda Chikondi 51</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Aggregate 2-2. Bata win on away goals rule</p>
<p>Champions' Cup</p>
<p>In Malabo: Cafe Band Sportif (Equatorial Guinea) 0 Munisport</p>
<p>(Congo) 1 (0-1).</p>
<p>Munisport win 5-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>Cup Winners' Cup</p>
<p>In Bata: Akonangui (Equatorial Guinea) 1 Renaissance (Chad)</p>
<p>4</p>
<p>Renaissance win 7-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>Champions' Cup</p>
<p>In Ouagadougou: Racing Club of Bobo-Dioulasso (Burkina Faso)</p>
<p>1 Junior Professionals (Liberia) 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Temani Traore 86</p>
<p>Junior Professionals win 2-1 on aggregate</p>
</text>
